{
  "_comment": "Declarative source of truth for offscript/scripts/check-capability-closure.ts. All paths are relative to the outer repository root (D:/offscript), not offscript/ \u2014 capability evidence (docs, code, tests) legitimately spans both. A dimension's value is an array of evidence pointers; the checker treats a REQUIRED dimension as satisfied iff at least one pointer resolves to a real file or directory on disk. A dimension may also carry a free-text mnemonic (e.g. a `/offscript <subcommand>` name) alongside its real backing path \u2014 only the real path needs to resolve. `types` declares, per capability type, whether each of the seven closure dimensions is required / optional / not-applicable for that type \u2014 derived from Offscript's actual capability shapes (see CAPABILITY-CLOSURE-REPORT.md Phase 3), not invented wholesale. A capability's `type` selects which row applies; CLI is not-applicable for internal-support and contract-only types, and not-applicable (by explicit repo convention \u2014 see docs/review, docs/execution) for engine-library types, matching the real, documented 'Review/Execution are library-level, no /offscript command surface yet' statements already in this repository.",
